<Wiki
  title="puv contain"
  description="Copy a Composer project into puv.toml and puv.lock without deleting the Composer files."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>contain</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv contain</code> imports the Composer project in the current directory. The walk
    around it is an <a href="/wiki/existing-project">existing project</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Keep the Composer files</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv contain
puv sync</pre>
  <p><code>require</code> and <code>require-dev</code> move into <code>puv.toml</code>.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      If <code>composer.lock</code> is present, that graph is copied into <code>puv.lock</code>
      and not resolved again.
    </li>
    <li>
      If <code>composer.lock</code> is missing, puv resolves from <code>composer.json</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Plain shell scripts are copied into <code>[scripts]</code>. PHP callables,
    <code>@composer</code> calls, and plugin events are skipped with a warning. The Composer
    files stay on disk.
  </p>
  <pre class="block">&#123;
  "require": &#123;
    "symfony/console": "^7.0"
  &#125;,
  "require-dev": &#123;
    "phpunit/phpunit": "^11.0"
  &#125;,
  "scripts": &#123;
    "test": "phpunit",
    "post-install-cmd": "@composer dump-autoload"
  &#125;
&#125;</pre>
  <p>That file becomes:</p>
  <pre class="block">[dependencies]
symfony/console = "^7.0"

[dev-dependencies]
phpunit/phpunit = "^11.0"

[scripts]
test = "phpunit"</pre>
  <p>
    <code>test</code> is a plain shell command, so it is copied.
    <code>post-install-cmd</code> calls <code>@composer</code>, so it is skipped and named in the
    warning. puv does not run scripts from the downloaded <code>composer.json</code> of a
    dependency either. That limit is <a href="/wiki/scope">scope</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete the Composer files</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv contain --clean</pre>
  <p>
    <code>--clean</code> is the form that removes the Composer files after the import. Without
    the flag they stay, so you can diff <code>puv.toml</code> against <code>composer.json</code>
    before you delete anything.
  </p>
  <p>
    Install the imported lock with <a href="/wiki/commands/sync"><code>puv sync</code></a>. It
    does not resolve again when the lock was copied.
  </p>
</Wiki>
